# Opening Bell Race

A premarket long-only ranking of stocks for the opening bell. Alpaca data (free plan: SIP 16 min delayed,
live prices only from the bell). Backend `app/` (port 11111, `npm run dev`); React board `trade/` (port 3000,
its own git repo). Read before changing anything:

- `docs/premarket-race.md` — every rule, the score formula, badges, filters, and why each exists.
- `docs/running-and-data.md` — running, replays, data quirks, code map, working notes.
- `app/config/race-rules.config.ts` — every threshold and scoring dial, with its math and calibration dates.

## How the trader works

- Rules must stay **modular and humanly readable**: one rule per object in `app/engine/race-rules/`, numbers
  only in the config, plain-language `describe()` text (it feeds the board's rule book).
- When given rough numbers ("0.2% below the high"), derive the right math (usually in daily ATRs) and
  calibrate on real days; put the calibration in the config comment.
- Minimal verification: typecheck (`npx tsc --noEmit -p .`), one quick check, move on. Keep waits short.
- Develop on a short list (~5 stocks). A **"full run"** = all stocks from 08:30:
  `npx ts-node scripts/mock-run.ts <date> 3 08:30 producion`, then report the final board.
- Stop a replay with `pkill -f "ts-node scripts/mock-run"` as a **separate** command before starting another.
- Badges: each has its own color, icon and tooltip (`trade/src/race/badges.js`, `race.css` `badge--<id>`).
  A solid fill = the strong form of a hue. Keep them distinct when adding new ones.
- Screenshot times are usually Israel time (New York + 7 h in summer).
- Never print or commit the Alpaca keys in `.env`.

## Score today

`100 × gapStrength × smaDistance × smaSlope (angle of the hourly 20 SMA) × holdQuality`, halved under the
hourly 200 SMA, halved while trading under the 20 SMA. After the bell everything is judged on the open.

